; atleastw_weight_overflow: the weight sum leaves the i64 range and must
; raise rather than wrap.
;
; weights = [2^62, 2^62, 2^62], k = 2^61, penalty = 0. The second partial
; sum is 2^63, which is not representable, so ATLEASTW raises
; ArithmeticOverflow before it derives a slack count from the total.
;
; The operands are chosen so the vector discriminates against the wrapping
; implementation instead of merely agreeing with the fixed one. Wrapped,
; the sum is -2^62, the excess is negative, no slack variables are
; allocated, the penalty of 0 emits nothing, and the program HALTs
; successfully with a size-3 all-zero model -- a silently wrong answer
; rather than a fault. A weight pair that overflows into a fault on the
; wrapping build would not have told those two implementations apart.

PUSH 3
BQMX r0

VECI r1
PUSH 0
VECPUSH r1
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r1
PUSH 2
VECPUSH r1

VECI r2
PUSH 4611686018427387904
VECPUSH r2
PUSH 4611686018427387904
VECPUSH r2
PUSH 4611686018427387904
VECPUSH r2

PUSH 2305843009213693952   ; k
PUSH 0                     ; penalty
ATLEASTW r0 r1 r2

HALT
